## Spec

1. **P2 — Bind historical beta attestation to approved manifest bytes.** `scripts/prepare-beta-attestation.mjs:65` hashes a fresh disk read after lines 38–56 validated and approved `manifestBytes`. Removing the detached signature eliminates the former consumer check against that original snapshot. Spec: #117 supersession says “Preserve ... immutable historical evidence ... publication-race safeguards”; PUBLIC_RELEASES.md Historical beta says approval binds `manifestSha256` and the “old manifest’s exact SHA-256/size.” Reproduced with the real legacy prepared fixture: intercept the approval-file read, replace only `release.json` with otherwise identical JSON changing `buildRunId` from 123 to 124, then run actual preparation. It exits 0 and emits the replacement manifest hash rather than the approved hash. Actual `verifyPublishedRelease` accepts run 124, while full prepared validation refuses it because retained provenance is run 123. Compute the emitted manifest record from the validated buffer; refuse a changed retained manifest before completing. Detailed runnable reproduction is alongside this report.

2. **P2 — Update the complete-shell F1 driver when deleting the fixture export.** `apps/desktop/test/shell-fixture.mjs:6–8` removes `keys`, but `apps/f1/test-drives/assets/desktop-shell-update.mjs:30–34` still imports it and uses it later. Spec: #116 shared acceptance requires “Use relevant F1 workflow/restart/update validation”; #121 requires successful/failed desktop updates. Repro: `F1_AGENT_MODE=mock node apps/f1/test-drives/assets/desktop-shell-update.mjs` exits immediately with `SyntaxError: ... does not provide an export named 'keys'`, before any assertion or service starts. Remove obsolete key wiring from the executable driver, or provide a maintained unsigned successor; preserve historical report/receipt bytes. Passing maintenance/lifecycle drives do not cover this broken complete-shell entry point.

